# CyberCheck fetcher VPN credentials.  ==>  copy to vpn.env, fill ONE provider block, then:  chmod 600 vpn.env
#
# vpn.env is gitignored (it matches *.env) and must be mode 600. It is read ONLY by the gluetun "vpn"
# service (fetcher/compose.yaml). The fetcher container never loads it.
#
# Pick an AUSTRALIAN exit: phishing kits that target Australian brands commonly cloak non-AU and
# datacenter IPs, so an AU egress is what gives the fetcher a realistic view. The fetcher checks the
# egress country against FETCH_EXPECTED_COUNTRY (default AU) before every fetch and fails closed if it
# does not match. All Mullvad/Proton AU relays are datacenter-hosted, so expect some kits to still show
# a decoy or nothing; that is recorded as inconclusive, never as "benign".
#
# Start:  docker compose --env-file .env --env-file vpn.env --profile fetch up -d
# Verify: ./scripts/verify-sandbox.sh

# ---- control-server API key (required: 32+ random letters/digits) --------------------------------
# Protects the gluetun control server so page JavaScript inside the namespace cannot drive the VPN.
# It is embedded in a JSON value, so use letters and digits only (no quotes/backslashes).
# Generate one:  openssl rand -hex 24
# The fetcher refuses to fetch if this is shorter than 16 chars or if the control server does not
# actually require it. It reaches the containers by interpolation, so always start the stack with
#   docker compose --env-file .env --env-file vpn.env --profile fetch up -d
GLUETUN_API_KEY=

# ============================================================================================
# Choose ONE provider block below. Delete or leave blank the others.
# ============================================================================================

# ---- Option A: Mullvad (WireGuard, Sydney) --------------------------------------------------
# Download a WireGuard config from https://mullvad.net/account/wireguard-config (pick an AU city).
# WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY is the [Interface] PrivateKey in that file (NOT the key shown on the Devices page).
# WIREGUARD_ADDRESSES is the [Interface] Address from that file (IPv4 only).
VPN_SERVICE_PROVIDER=mullvad
VPN_TYPE=wireguard
WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY=
WIREGUARD_ADDRESSES=
SERVER_COUNTRIES=Australia
SERVER_CITIES=Sydney
# GLUETUN_UPDATER_PERIOD=24h   # keep the bundled AU relay list fresh (set in fetcher/compose.yaml env)

# ---- Option B: your own VPS (custom WireGuard) ----------------------------------------------
# Use a VPS you control as the exit. WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_IP must be the VPS public IPv4 (a hostname is
# NOT accepted, and it is not the tailnet IP). On the VPS, firewall wg0 FORWARD so it cannot reach
# 10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16, 100.64/10, 169.254/16 or fc00::/7, drop NEW INPUT from wg0, and do not
# run Tailscale subnet routing there.
# VPN_SERVICE_PROVIDER=custom
# VPN_TYPE=wireguard
# WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_IP=
# WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_PORT=51820
# WIREGUARD_PUBLIC_KEY=
# WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY=
# WIREGUARD_PRESHARED_KEY=
# WIREGUARD_ADDRESSES=10.13.13.2/32
# WIREGUARD_PERSISTENT_KEEPALIVE_INTERVAL=25s

# ---- Option C: ProtonVPN (WireGuard, Sydney; paid plan only, no AU free server) -------------
# WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY comes from Proton's WireGuard config page. Do NOT set WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_PORT.
# VPN_SERVICE_PROVIDER=protonvpn
# VPN_TYPE=wireguard
# WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY=
# WIREGUARD_ADDRESSES=10.2.0.2/32
# SERVER_COUNTRIES=Australia
# SERVER_CITIES=Sydney
# SECURE_CORE_ONLY=off
# FREE_ONLY=off
# VPN_PORT_FORWARDING=off
# Leave GLUETUN_UPDATER_PERIOD unset for Proton unless you also set UPDATER_PROTONVPN_EMAIL/PASSWORD.
